{
  "analysis": "Python3 is not available, but Perl, awk, and apt-get are available on Ubuntu 24.04. To satisfy the requirement that `oligotm` is ground truth, I should try to install primer3 tools via apt. I also need to parse/compare sequences; Perl can do that if Python is unavailable.",
  "plan": "Check apt package availability for primer3/oligotm, and use a Perl one-liner to parse the FASTA and report sequence lengths plus BsaI sites. This will guide both tool installation and primer design.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-cache search primer3\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "perl -e 'open F,\"sequences.fasta\"; while(<F>){chomp; if(/^>(\\S+)/){$n=$1} else {$s{$n}.=uc($_)}} for $k (keys %s){print \"$k \",length($s{$k}),\"\\n\"; for $site (qw(GGTCTC GAGACC)){@p=(); for $i(0..length($s{$k})-6){push @p,$i+1 if substr($s{$k},$i,6) eq $site} print \"  $site @p\\n\"}}'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
 "task_complete": false
}
